  "notes": {
    "title": {
      "kind": "title1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -300,
      "maxW": 4240,
      "text": "Tasks · When and Deadline at a glance"
    },
    "howto": {
      "x": -560,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 480,
      "size": 24,
      "text": "How to try it\n\n• Press Play, then click inside once so it has the keys.\n• Picked: the When is quiet grey text and only a deadline is a capsule; an overdue task's checkbox ring is red.\n• Proposed, on the strip: Wording, Due today, When today. The defaults are the recommendations.\n• Hover a date for its full date; click it for the popover. Narrow the window: the When gives way, a deadline always stays."
    },
    "t_cues": {
      "kind": "title1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 900,
      "maxW": 2880,
      "text": "1 · Cues on the checkbox (proposed)"
    },
    "n_cues": {
      "x": -560,
      "y": 1200,
      "w": 480,
      "size": 24,
      "text": "The ring carries the deadline: red when it's past (picked), amber when it's today. A deadline is one or the other, never both.\n\nWhen today (a task on today's plate, seen in a list) is a 4pt dot in Today's yellow, inside the ring. Recommended: it's a different shape from the rings, so it sits with either; amber already means today (the capsule, the ring, Today's sun).\n\nThe blue ring reads like the blue of a checked box and has to give way to a deadline's ring. The fill nearly vanishes in dark and reads as pressed."
    },
    "n_cues2": {
      "x": -560,
      "y": 4360,
      "w": 480,
      "size": 24,
      "text": "Today shows the rings but never the dot: everything there is on today's plate. Upcoming and Undated have nothing for today. Done and Trash rows show no cue.\n\nSelection keeps both (the fill is behind them). The checkbox's label reads the cue aloud: “Complete: ECE 358 lab report, overdue, planned for today”."
    },
    "t_words": {
      "kind": "title1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 5360,
      "maxW": 5320,
      "text": "2 · Wording: “Nd left”, the user's countdown (proposed)"
    },
    "n_words": {
      "x": -560,
      "y": 5660,
      "w": 480,
      "size": 24,
      "text": "A deadline counts the whole days left, not the deadline's own day: “13d left” … “1d left”, then “Due today”, then “1d late”.\n\nFar off, it counts in weeks from 14 days (“2w left”), months from 60 (“2mo left”), years from 365, always rounded down, so it never shows more time than there is.\n\nOverdue: “2d late” (recommended) over “2d over” (it reads as “over budget”, and as “finished”) and “2d ago” (it says when, not that you're late).\n\nThe When is a plan, not a countdown: “Today”, “Tomorrow”, then “in 2d”, “in 3w”. Never “left”."
    },
    "t_views": {
      "kind": "title1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 9020,
      "maxW": 3240,
      "text": "Views and narrow widths"
    },
    "t_detail": {
      "kind": "title1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 10060,
      "maxW": 4240,
      "text": "The detail pane and the popover"
    }
  }
